  "observations": [
    "Stationary panoramic pixels remain exactly unchanged through twenty zero-advance passes.",
    "In the renderer reference test, positive-advance texture warps differ by at most one RGB byte on the smooth calibration fixture, across three view orientations. This validates mapping geometry, not preservation of arbitrary image detail through repeated resampling.",
    "Visual review of the motion-only sequence shows foreground approach rather than the old repeated screenshot-placement stretching.",
    "Arches develops repeated curved ribbing; Organic develops branching cellular structure. These outputs come from the actual Inception objectives with no authored glitch effects.",
    "Low-resolution source detail still softens during approach. The experiment transforms an existing scene and does not yet establish fresh area generation or indefinite visual novelty."
  ],
  "nextSteps": [
